1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,379
Two independent CCPad windows.

2
00:00:03,389 --> 00:00:07,932
On the left, a travel story; on the right, sample sales data.

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:11,794
I submit a task in each window.

4
00:00:11,804 --> 00:00:16,191
Both Codex sessions run at once, and both lights turn green.

5
00:00:17,467 --> 00:00:20,386
The last instruction stays visible here.

6
00:00:20,396 --> 00:00:23,965
Click to copy it, and quickly recall what you asked.

7
00:00:25,233 --> 00:00:29,030
One session writes the story while the other totals sales.

8
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:32,573
Both tasks progress together in this real recording.

9
00:00:33,833 --> 00:00:37,630
Yellow means the tasks are finished and waiting for input.

10
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:40,608
The story and sales summary are saved.

11
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:44,590
Now I exit Codex on the right.

12
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:48,747
Red means it's closed; the left session remains available.

13
00:00:50,033 --> 00:00:54,214
See each task, its status, and its last instruction.

14
00:00:54,224 --> 00:00:58,191
CCPad makes parallel AI work easy to follow.
